Subject: [PATCH] Allow more time for the rotation test TLS handshake

TestSVIDRotation generates an agent SVID with a three-second lifetime.
The mock clock is truncated to a whole second, but the TLS server uses
wall-clock time. On slow or busy workers the SVID can expire before the
initial handshake, failing manager initialization with "tls: expired
certificate" before any rotation assertions run.

Allow a minute for the handshake. The test derives its rotation interval
and advances its mock clock from the same TTL, preserving the rotation
checks without waiting for the longer lifetime in real time.

--- a/pkg/agent/manager/manager_test.go
+++ b/pkg/agent/manager/manager_test.go
@@ -441,7 +441,9 @@
 
 	clk := clock.NewMock(t)
 
-	baseTTLSeconds := 3
+	// Allow slow build workers to complete the initial TLS handshake.
+	// Rotation uses the mock clock, so a longer TTL does not slow the test.
+	baseTTLSeconds := 60
 	api := newMockAPI(t, &mockAPIConfig{
 		km: km,
 		getAuthorizedEntries: func(*mockAPI, int32, *entryv1.GetAuthorizedEntriesRequest) (*entryv1.GetAuthorizedEntriesResponse, error) {
